    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d905">

                <pb facs="0931" n="843" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg843"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr. Jay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-11-04"><hi rendition="#italic">November 4,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 718.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of Mr.
                    Leishman’s No. 912, of the 13th ultimo, in further relation to the proposed new
                    stamp law.</p>
                <p>Mr. Leishman’s course in protesting to the Turkish Government against the
                    imposition of such a tax upon American citizens in Turkey is approved.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. B. Loomis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
